      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It has been demonstrated in experiments on nonanesthetized intact and spinalized cats that intrathecal morphine increased blood pressure and renal nerve sympathetic activity and enhanced the nociceptive reactions. It is suggested that morphine plays an essential role in the effect of propriospinal system on the generation of sympathetic spinal reflexes."},
